  "user_prompt": "EARLIER: the end of Episode 2, from 74.2 s (block ids carry their episode)\nE002-B031 74.3-76.4 NORA (Quiet, Dangerous): Dev. Look at me.\nE002-B032 76.6-81.9 [camera] Wide shot of the booth: Dev reaching for the door, Hollis blocking it.\nE002-B033 76.9-78.9 [action] Dev lunges for the door; Hollis plants a hand on his chest.\nE002-B034 79.2-81.7 HOLLIS (Smug): Nobody leaves while we're live.\nE002-B035 81.9-84.9 [camera] Close-up on the security monitor: the lobby is empty, the front door swinging shut.\nE002-B036 82.2-83.7 [sound] The door buzzer cuts off mid-tone.\nE002-B037 84.9-89.1 [camera] Close-up on Nora, staring at the monitor through the glass.\nE002-B038 85.2-88.9 THE CALLER [V.O.] (Whispering, Close): Second floor, Nora. Third door on the left.\nE002-B039 89.1-94.9 [camera] Slow push-in on the studio door as its handle begins to turn.\nE002-B040 89.4-91.9 [action] The studio door handle turns slowly.\nE002-B041 92.2-94.7 [sound] The synth climbs into a sharp cliffhanger sting.\nE002-B042 94.9-96.4 [camera] Cut to black.\n\nEPISODE 3 (96.5 s)\n\n== Scene 1: INT. HARBOR FM – STUDIO B – CONTINUOUS ==\nB001 0-2.5 [camera] Close-up on the turning handle.\nB002 0.3-1.5 [action] The door swings open.\nB003 2.5-6 [camera] Wide shot: a woman in a yellow raincoat stands dripping in the doorway, her phone glowing in her hand.\nB004 2.8-5.8 [sound] Rain roars in the stairwell behind her.\nB005 6-8.5 [camera] Close-up on Nora, backing against the desk.\nB006 6.3-7.9 NORA (Terrified): Who are you?\nB007 8.5-17.1 [camera] Close-up on the woman as she lowers her hood.\nB008 8.8-10.8 [action] The woman lowers her hood; a pale scar runs along her jaw.\nB009 11.1-16.9 WOMAN IN YELLOW RAINCOAT (Steady, Hurt): You knew me as Maya. You held on to me in the river.\nB010 17.1-22.2 [camera] Extreme close-up on Nora's face.\nB011 17.4-22 NORA (Stunned, Whispering): Maya Cole? They never found you. They said you drowned.\nB012 22.2-31.9 [camera] Two-shot of Nora and Maya.\nB013 22.5-31.7 MAYA (Bitter): I washed up two miles downstream. Someone drove onto that bridge with no lights, and drove away when I went over.\nB014 31.9-34.9 [camera] Through the glass, Dev backs away from the window.\nB015 32.2-34.7 [sound] A low heartbeat pulse.\nB016 34.9-42.5 [camera] Medium shot of Nora turning to the glass.\nB017 35.2-42.3 NORA (Breaking): You told me it was my fault. You said I panicked and let go of her.\n\n== Scene 2: INT. HARBOR FM – CONTROL BOOTH – CONTINUOUS ==\nB018 42.5-45 [camera] Nora storms into the booth.\nB019 42.8-44 [action] Nora shoves the booth door open.\nB020 45-50.5 [camera] Close-up on Dev.\nB021 45.3-50.3 DEV (Desperate, Pleading): I was nineteen. I'd been drinking. I thought she was gone.\nB022 50.5-52.5 [camera] Close-up on Nora.\nB023 50.8-51.6 [action] Nora slaps Dev across the face.\nB024 52.5-55 [camera] Close-up on Dev, his cheek reddening.\nB025 52.8-54.3 [sound] The slap rings out over the live microphone.\nB026 55-60.5 [camera] Medium shot of Nora, tears on her face.\nB027 55.3-60.3 NORA (Furious, Tearful): Ten years. Ten years I carried her, and you let me.\nB028 60.5-64 [camera] Hollis, giddy, holds up his phone to show a live listener graph.\nB029 60.8-63.7 HOLLIS (Delighted): Keep going. Sixty thousand and climbing.\nB030 64-73.7 [camera] Close-up on Maya in the booth doorway.\nB031 64.3-73.5 MAYA (Cold): Turn it off, Mr. Hollis. Or tell them how much you paid to keep your nephew's car out of the papers.\nB032 73.7-76.2 [camera] Extreme close-up on Hollis, his smile frozen.\nB033 74-75.5 [sound] A sharp string sting.\nB034 76.2-80.9 [camera] Close-up on Nora.\nB035 76.5-80.7 NORA (Slow, Realising): Your nephew. You hired him knowing what he did.\nB036 80.9-84.4 [camera] Wide shot of the booth as blue and red lights sweep across the window.\nB037 81.2-84.2 [sound] Police sirens rise outside.\nB038 84.4-92 [camera] Close-up on Hollis, slipping his phone into his coat.\nB039 84.7-91.8 HOLLIS (Cold, Threatening): Say one more word on air, and none of you will ever work in radio again.\nB040 92-95 [camera] Extreme close-up on Nora's hand moving to the master fader.\nB041 92.3-94.8 [sound] The synth hits a cliffhanger high and holds it.\nB042 95-96.5 [camera] Cut to black.\n\nCLIPS\nC1: 50.5-75.5 s (25.0 s). Hook options: B022, B023, B024, B025. Ending options: B030, B031, B032, B033.\nC2: 6-34.7 s (28.7 s). Hook options: B005, B006, B007, B008. Ending options: B012, B013, B014, B015.\nC3: 42.5-75.5 s (33.0 s). Hook options: B018, B019, B020, B021. Ending options: B030, B031, B032, B033.\nC4, 2 parts: 6-16.9 s, then 64-75.5 s (22.4 s in all). Hook options: B005, B006, B007, B008. Ending options: B030, B031, B032, B033.\nC5, 2 parts: Episode 2 79.2-96.4 s, then 0-7.9 s (25.1 s in all). Hook options: E002-B034, E002-B035, E002-B036. Ending options: B001, B003, B004, B005, B006.",
